<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87790" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκινδῡνεύω</span></b> , pf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κεκινδύνευκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					9(2).531.5
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Larissa</span>):—<i>run risk
				before</i> others, <i>brave the first danger, bear the brunt
				of battle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.208
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. στρατευόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.24
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τοῦ πλήθους</span>
			<i>brave danger for</i> the people, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Hier.</u>
				10.8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῷ βαρβάρῳ</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς Ἑλλάδος</span>) <i>braved</i>
			him <i>for</i> Greece (or, <i>first of all</i>), <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.73
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὑπέρ τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					7.3.31
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Dem.Fr.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ τῆς Ἑλλάδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					4.75
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ τῆς ἐλευθερίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					18.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τῆς ἐλευθερίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					9.38.4
				</span></i>
			: c. dat. modi, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τοῖς μεγίστοις ἀγῶσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pel.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τοῖς Ἴβηρσι</span>
			<i>open the engagement</i> with them, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.113.9
			</span></i>.</div>
